# Site configuration for the benchmark SLURM scripts. Copy to `benchmark/slurm/site.env` (which is
# gitignored) and fill in the paths of this machine. Nothing tracked in the repository may name a
# path of one machine, so every such path lives here.
#
# `common.sh` sources this file; every variable is exported to the Julia processes it launches.

# Julia. Either name the binary, or the juliaup depot whose newest `julia-*/bin/julia` to use. Do
# not point this at the login-node `julia` wrapper: it applies its own `taskset` over a random core
# window, which fails inside a SLURM cgroup.
#JULIA_BIN=/path/to/julia-1.12.x/bin/julia
JULIAUP_DEPOT_PATH=/path/to/juliaup_depot

# BART builds timed by the comparison suite, one per BLAS backend. BART 1.0 dispatches on the name it
# is called by, so each build must keep the file name `bart` (one directory per build). It needs
# GCC 12 or newer, and on Red Hat a non-OpenBLAS build links ATLAS unless `LDFLAGS` is overridden.
RISTRETTO_BENCH_BART_OPENBLAS=/path/to/bart-openblas/bart
RISTRETTO_BENCH_BART_MKL=/path/to/bart-mkl/bart
# The BART build a `--device=cuda` comparison times (`pics -g`): built with `CUDA = 1`, OpenBLAS
# (a GPU run uses OpenBLAS as the host BLAS) and the GPU's own architecture in `GPUARCH_FLAGS`
# (`-gencode arch=compute_80,code=sm_80` on an A100).
#RISTRETTO_BENCH_BART_CUDA=/path/to/bart-cuda/bart

# The Python interpreter (Python >= 3.10) that PythonCall runs SigPy and MRpro in. See
# benchmark/comparison/README.md.
RISTRETTO_BENCH_SIGPY_PYTHON=/path/to/venvs/py314/bin/python
# The interpreter of a `--device=cuda` comparison: the GPU builds of PyTorch and CuPy, with SigPy
# and MRpro. Unset, a GPU run uses RISTRETTO_BENCH_SIGPY_PYTHON.
#RISTRETTO_BENCH_GPU_PYTHON=/path/to/venvs/py314-gpu/bin/python

# Where MRITestData downloads and caches real scanner data (several GB with fastMRI breast).
RISTRETTO_BENCH_DATA_DIR=/path/to/MRITestData/cache
# Where prepared real-data cases (k-space, ESPIRiT maps, reference) are cached between processes.
# Default: <download directory>/ristretto_benchmark.
#RISTRETTO_BENCH_WORK_DIR=/path/to/ristretto_benchmark

# MRITestData's gated source (fastMRI) is used only when its files are already cached here or
# signed download URLs are registered with `MRITestData.set_fastmri_urls!(email_text)` in the
# benchmark environment (they are stored in its gitignored LocalPreferences.toml, never here).

# Partitions. `submit.sh` uses the test partition unless it is given `--production`.
SLURM_TEST_PARTITION=test
SLURM_PRODUCTION_PARTITION=cpu
# Where `--production` sends a script that asks for a GPU (`#SBATCH --gres=gpu...`).
SLURM_GPU_PARTITION=gpu
#SLURM_ACCOUNT=...
